      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 102, Mexican feather grass. Care: NC State, Missouri BG and RHS agree on full sun, free drainage and drought tolerance; NC State and Missouri BG both say it may go dormant in summer drought and that it seeds freely (weedy; invasive in Australia and parts of California). Size: NC State and Missouri BG give 30 to 60 cm by 30 to 60 cm; RHS says up to 1 m tall by 0.5 m, so 60 by 60 cm is kept. Hardiness H4 is the RHS rating (it lists the plant as Stipa tenuissima under its accepted name; the Nassella page was read). Growth rate medium is NC State alone. Toxicity: no page read states any, no ASPCA page, so people and pets are unknown. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
